1
00:00:44,737 --> 00:00:48,550
It took us a long time to get here.

2
00:00:50,997 --> 00:00:54,711
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.

3
00:00:54,711 --> 00:00:58,881
I won't make you wait again.

4
00:00:58,881 --> 00:01:00,408
Ever.

5
00:01:38,341 --> 00:01:40,141
<i>Woo Jae?</i>

6
00:01:40,793 --> 00:01:42,037
<i>What?</i>

7
00:01:42,037 --> 00:01:43,334
<i>Is this a dream?</i>

8
00:01:47,089 --> 00:01:48,400
<i>He's warm...</i>

9
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,459
<i>This isn't a dream.</i>

10
00:01:52,743 --> 00:01:54,554
<i>It's me!</i>

11
00:01:54,554 --> 00:01:56,063
<i>This is my body.</i>

12
00:01:56,063 --> 00:01:58,088
<i>What's going on?</i>

13
00:01:58,088 --> 00:02:00,878
<i>Am I back? Why now?</i>

14
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:04,959
Cut.

15
00:02:05,565 --> 00:02:06,661
What was that?

16
00:02:06,661 --> 00:02:08,707
Did she just look at the camera?

17
00:02:09,387 --> 00:02:12,024
What's wrong, Ha Na?

18
00:02:12,024 --> 00:02:14,048
<i>I'm really Yoon Ha Na...</i>

19
00:02:14,048 --> 00:02:17,473
<i>And I'm filming with him right now?</i>

20
00:02:17,473 --> 00:02:19,385
Hey. What's wrong?

21
00:02:20,395 --> 00:02:22,596
Oh... well...

22
00:02:22,596 --> 00:02:23,700
<i>Come on, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

23
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:25,753
<i>Think! Make something up!</i>

24
00:02:25,753 --> 00:02:27,129
A spider!

25
00:02:27,129 --> 00:02:28,249
It's gone now.

26
00:02:28,249 --> 00:02:30,225
That scared me. Sorry.

27
00:02:30,225 --> 00:02:31,559
Jeez, you scared me.

28
00:02:31,559 --> 00:02:32,803
Let's go again.

29
00:02:32,803 --> 00:02:33,996
Okay.

30
00:02:49,491 --> 00:02:50,682
<i>How did this happen?</i>

31
00:02:50,682 --> 00:02:53,611
<i>Did I get my career back as the lead?</i>

32
00:02:53,611 --> 00:02:55,165
Let's do it.

33
00:02:55,165 --> 00:02:56,612
Ready...

34
00:02:58,764 --> 00:03:00,075
Action.

35
00:03:01,257 --> 00:03:03,218
[Haesol Namchon]

36
00:03:03,218 --> 00:03:06,671
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.

37
00:03:06,671 --> 00:03:10,788
I won't make you wait again.

38
00:03:10,788 --> 00:03:12,373
Ever.

39
00:03:35,849 --> 00:03:37,381
[Episode 11]

40
00:03:49,103 --> 00:03:50,966
This is so much fun!

41
00:03:53,267 --> 00:03:54,410
Let's toast!

42
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:56,069
Cheers!

43
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,750
Nice work.

44
00:04:00,064 --> 00:04:01,407
What? Why?

45
00:04:01,407 --> 00:04:03,431
No actresses, no anchors,

46
00:04:03,431 --> 00:04:05,534
not even a chaebol heiress?

47
00:04:05,534 --> 00:04:07,251
No, thanks.

48
00:04:07,251 --> 00:04:09,804
The women already in my life
are enough of a headache.

49
00:04:09,804 --> 00:04:11,234
- Dae Jun!
- Yes?

50
00:04:11,234 --> 00:04:12,631
- Come here.
- What?

51
00:04:12,631 --> 00:04:13,838
Talk some sense into him.

52
00:04:13,838 --> 00:04:15,526
You still don't get it?

53
00:04:15,526 --> 00:04:17,207
Ha Ru's got women lined up.

54
00:04:17,207 --> 00:04:18,430
It's not just gossip.

55
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:21,430
He hasn't called anyone his girlfriend
in ten years. Not since S.

56
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:23,080
- Come on, man.
- Oh, sorry.

57
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,607
- Sorry.
- "S?"

58
00:04:24,607 --> 00:04:26,644
Who was she?

59
00:04:26,644 --> 00:04:28,104
Your first love?

60
00:04:28,104 --> 00:04:29,527
- Come on, Dae Jun. Spill!
- No way.

61
00:04:29,527 --> 00:04:30,828
You're better off not knowing.

62
00:04:30,828 --> 00:04:32,018
Just enjoy the moment!

63
00:04:32,018 --> 00:04:32,978
Whatever.

64
00:04:32,978 --> 00:04:34,742
Mind setting me up instead?

65
00:04:34,742 --> 00:04:35,988
Seriously?

66
00:04:35,988 --> 00:04:38,068
There he is. Chef Yoon's human shield.

67
00:04:38,068 --> 00:04:41,118
Chef Yoon's on a roll right now.

68
00:04:41,118 --> 00:04:43,888
Between the restaurant and his shoots,

69
00:04:43,888 --> 00:04:45,625
he barely has time to date.

70
00:04:45,625 --> 00:04:47,298
I see.

71
00:04:47,298 --> 00:04:48,972
You always take his side.

72
00:04:48,972 --> 00:04:50,109
Yeah.

73
00:04:50,109 --> 00:04:53,602
Must be nice having someone like him
in your corner.

74
00:04:53,602 --> 00:04:55,546
Yeah, it is.

75
00:04:55,546 --> 00:04:56,797
Yeah!

76
00:04:56,797 --> 00:04:59,910
- All right, chefs! Great work!
- Cheers.

77
00:05:02,071 --> 00:05:03,692
Excuse me.

78
00:05:07,746 --> 00:05:12,157
Chef Hong is totally wasted
and asking for you guys.

79
00:05:12,898 --> 00:05:14,341
Dae Jun, let's go.

80
00:05:14,341 --> 00:05:16,401
What the heck...

81
00:05:16,401 --> 00:05:17,708
I'll be right back.

82
00:05:19,695 --> 00:05:21,067
Hey!

83
00:05:21,067 --> 00:05:22,250
Oh, you...

84
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:23,709
Chef.

85
00:05:26,341 --> 00:05:28,251
Pyo Gyeong Woo?

86
00:05:28,251 --> 00:05:30,364
Wait... I'm a chef?

87
00:05:30,364 --> 00:05:31,522
What?

88
00:05:32,110 --> 00:05:33,895
Are you drunk, bro?

89
00:05:34,537 --> 00:05:35,986
"Bro?"

90
00:05:40,530 --> 00:05:42,120
<i>This is my body!</i>

91
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:46,654
<i>2026...</i>

92
00:05:46,654 --> 00:05:48,847
<i>Why now?</i>

93
00:05:48,847 --> 00:05:50,250
<i>What happened?</i>

94
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:51,310
Hey, bro.

95
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:52,706
You'd better be ready for a long night.

96
00:05:52,706 --> 00:05:55,314
- You won 500 million won.
- "500 million won?"

97
00:05:55,314 --> 00:05:58,425
Everyone says you're not going home tonight.

98
00:05:58,425 --> 00:06:00,298
Brace yourself.

99
00:06:01,393 --> 00:06:02,966
[Yoon Ha Na]
<i>Where are you?</i>

100
00:06:06,327 --> 00:06:07,925
Hi, Ha Ru.

101
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,951
Hi.

102
00:06:10,951 --> 00:06:12,530
Who are you again?

103
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:14,200
Is that a joke?

104
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,666
Why are you being so cute?

105
00:06:17,133 --> 00:06:19,213
Oh, yeah. I'm pretty cute.

106
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:20,914
What's with you?

107
00:06:20,914 --> 00:06:23,839
Since when are you so formal with me?

108
00:06:23,839 --> 00:06:26,136
Oh, right.

109
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:29,064
Guess I wasn't this polite before.

110
00:06:29,064 --> 00:06:32,333
I kind of like you being all polite.

111
00:06:34,387 --> 00:06:37,432
This is what I like about you, Ha Ru.

112
00:06:37,432 --> 00:06:39,856
You act all cold and tough,

113
00:06:39,856 --> 00:06:42,931
then you give me those innocent eyes.

114
00:06:42,931 --> 00:06:45,748
Want to come to my place tonight?

115
00:06:45,748 --> 00:06:48,472
Your place?

116
00:06:48,472 --> 00:06:49,816
<i>Yoon Ha Ru, you psycho...</i>

117
00:06:49,816 --> 00:06:53,321
<i>What the hell have you
been doing with your life?</i>

118
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:55,820
Good to see you!

119
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:57,699
- Oh, Gyeong Woo...
- How have you been?

120
00:06:57,699 --> 00:06:59,275
You got even prettier.

121
00:06:59,275 --> 00:07:01,985
- How do you always look so good?
- I'll get going!

122
00:07:01,985 --> 00:07:04,084
Come over here.

123
00:07:25,758 --> 00:07:27,269
<i>I love you.</i>

124
00:07:33,554 --> 00:07:35,738
Get a grip, Yoon Ha Na!

125
00:07:35,738 --> 00:07:39,502
I need to get it together...

126
00:07:56,515 --> 00:07:59,032
You okay?

127
00:07:59,032 --> 00:08:00,716
Of course.

128
00:08:00,716 --> 00:08:02,638
I'm more than okay.

129
00:08:04,421 --> 00:08:06,051
Doesn't look like it.

130
00:08:06,051 --> 00:08:08,225
You feel warm...

131
00:08:08,225 --> 00:08:09,675
<i>What's wrong with you, Yoon Ha Na?</i>

132
00:08:09,675 --> 00:08:11,550
<i>You're not a teenager anymore...</i>

133
00:08:14,088 --> 00:08:16,112
Looks like I'll be here all night.

134
00:08:16,112 --> 00:08:18,086
Text me when you get home.

135
00:08:18,086 --> 00:08:21,036
And if you start feeling sick,
call me right away.

136
00:08:21,036 --> 00:08:22,889
Okay. Don't worry.

137
00:08:22,889 --> 00:08:24,109
Yeah.

138
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:36,433
Good work, Kkomi.

139
00:08:38,447 --> 00:08:39,853
Oh my.

140
00:08:41,141 --> 00:08:43,061
Stand by, please!

141
00:08:44,707 --> 00:08:46,396
- Go on.
- Yeah.

142
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,913
Good to see you, Ha Na.

143
00:09:04,657 --> 00:09:05,982
What?

144
00:09:05,982 --> 00:09:09,821
We've been filming together all day...
What's with "good to see you?"

145
00:09:09,821 --> 00:09:12,265
And what's with "Kkomi?"

146
00:09:12,265 --> 00:09:14,994
Must be his pet name for me.

147
00:09:14,994 --> 00:09:16,612
That's so cute.

148
00:09:16,612 --> 00:09:19,504
I'm seriously losing it.

149
00:09:21,434 --> 00:09:23,151
Ha Na?

150
00:09:23,151 --> 00:09:24,428
Yeah.

151
00:09:24,428 --> 00:09:26,116
Let's go, Seok Min.

152
00:09:36,078 --> 00:09:39,417
Only one month till the final shoot.

153
00:09:41,972 --> 00:09:47,597
Ha Na. Shouldn't we start
picking out your red-carpet dress?

154
00:09:47,597 --> 00:09:51,401
What? We haven't even finished the movie yet.

155
00:09:51,401 --> 00:09:54,465
I'm telling you,
this could be the role of your career.

156
00:09:54,465 --> 00:09:56,631
And it's not just me.

157
00:09:56,631 --> 00:10:01,297
Everyone says once this comes out,
Best Actress is yours.

158
00:10:01,297 --> 00:10:02,792
Best Actress?

159
00:10:02,792 --> 00:10:07,954
Other actors get one big break
and start racking up trophies.

160
00:10:07,954 --> 00:10:10,324
But you always get Popularity Awards.

161
00:10:10,324 --> 00:10:13,005
It drives me crazy.

162
00:10:14,611 --> 00:10:15,616
Still...

163
00:10:15,616 --> 00:10:19,824
Woo Jae and Jun Mo teamed up
and said the role had to be yours.

164
00:10:19,824 --> 00:10:24,041
They didn't even send the script
to any other actresses.

165
00:10:24,041 --> 00:10:25,227
That's pretty touching.

166
00:10:25,227 --> 00:10:28,427
<i>They teamed up?</i>

167
00:10:28,427 --> 00:10:30,989
Oh, right...

168
00:10:41,431 --> 00:10:42,709
<i>The camcorder...</i>

169
00:10:42,709 --> 00:10:44,251
<i>It's gone.</i>

170
00:10:54,075 --> 00:10:55,833
As you can see...

171
00:10:55,833 --> 00:10:59,395
We found bugs and tracking devices

172
00:10:59,395 --> 00:11:04,761
in the living room, kitchen, bedroom, and car.

173
00:11:04,761 --> 00:11:08,794
I bet there's more if we keep looking.

174
00:11:08,794 --> 00:11:09,819
Wow...

175
00:11:09,819 --> 00:11:15,087
So this really does happen
in celebrities' homes.

176
00:11:15,087 --> 00:11:16,118
Hey, look at this.

177
00:11:16,118 --> 00:11:17,457
- She's pretty, right?
- I don't know...

178
00:11:17,457 --> 00:11:21,255
So Ha Na's still the target.

179
00:11:21,255 --> 00:11:23,121
- She's pretty.
- Not really.

180
00:11:24,117 --> 00:11:27,800
Whoever planted them
will know they've gone dead.

181
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,876
They'll probably make another move soon.

182
00:11:31,628 --> 00:11:33,732
Good.

183
00:11:33,732 --> 00:11:36,502
I've been wanting to see who's behind this.

184
00:11:36,502 --> 00:11:38,605
- Okay.
- Yeah...

185
00:11:50,199 --> 00:11:51,550
It's Yoon Ha Na!

186
00:11:51,550 --> 00:11:53,349
No way!

187
00:11:53,349 --> 00:11:54,506
- Wow!
- Hello.

188
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:55,847
- I'm...
- Move over!

189
00:11:55,847 --> 00:11:57,547
I'm Lee Gyeong Min.

190
00:11:57,547 --> 00:11:59,262
Come take a picture of us.

191
00:11:59,262 --> 00:12:00,641
Mind if I put my arm around you?

192
00:12:00,641 --> 00:12:01,805
- Sure.
- Thank you.

193
00:12:01,805 --> 00:12:04,278
- Hurry up and take it.
- A picture? Okay.

194
00:12:04,278 --> 00:12:06,015
Chef, could you take our picture?

195
00:12:06,015 --> 00:12:08,299
- Just take mine...
- Hold on!

196
00:12:08,299 --> 00:12:10,797
- What the...
- Could you take a picture for us?

197
00:12:10,797 --> 00:12:12,762
Just the three of us, please.

198
00:12:12,762 --> 00:12:13,775
Just us.

199
00:12:13,775 --> 00:12:15,235
- Just the three of us.
- You can step out.

200
00:12:15,235 --> 00:12:16,695
- The three of us.
- Not you.

201
00:12:16,695 --> 00:12:18,053
Yeah, yeah.

202
00:12:18,053 --> 00:12:19,320
All right, here we go.

203
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:22,207
One, two, three.

204
00:12:26,554 --> 00:12:28,477
So... what's going on?

205
00:12:28,477 --> 00:12:31,010
That's what I'm asking.

206
00:12:31,964 --> 00:12:33,134
The camcorder!

207
00:12:33,134 --> 00:12:35,200
It was in your room.

208
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:38,136
Weren't you and Woo Jae the only ones home?

209
00:12:38,136 --> 00:12:41,345
What? You think Woo Jae took the battery out?

210
00:12:41,345 --> 00:12:42,476
Why would he?

211
00:12:42,476 --> 00:12:43,904
How would I know?

212
00:12:43,904 --> 00:12:46,004
You were the one with him.

213
00:12:46,663 --> 00:12:48,644
What changed this time?

214
00:12:48,644 --> 00:12:51,410
Why did the camcorder disappear?

215
00:12:51,410 --> 00:12:53,360
The last video you recorded...

216
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:55,480
was in 2017.

217
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,543
Our last time jump...

218
00:12:57,543 --> 00:12:59,642
Maybe it disappeared once its job was done.

219
00:12:59,642 --> 00:13:02,498
And that's why
we're not switching bodies anymore?

220
00:13:02,498 --> 00:13:04,077
Who knows?

221
00:13:04,077 --> 00:13:06,245
Maybe there's another rule.

222
00:13:06,245 --> 00:13:08,566
Or maybe the magic just wore off.

223
00:13:09,644 --> 00:13:10,662
Anyway...

224
00:13:10,662 --> 00:13:12,915
Woo Jae's alive, and you two are together.

225
00:13:12,915 --> 00:13:14,752
And you...

226
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:17,418
You're not back where you were,
but you're doing better than last time.

227
00:13:17,418 --> 00:13:20,456
You're getting lead roles again
instead of being stuck in supporting roles.

228
00:13:20,456 --> 00:13:24,435
And you're a famous chef now...

229
00:13:24,435 --> 00:13:26,903
So we're good. Right?

230
00:13:26,903 --> 00:13:31,443
First, I need to sort things out with Ye Rang.

231
00:13:37,939 --> 00:13:39,291
[Boss]
[No search results]

232
00:13:42,523 --> 00:13:43,832
[CEO Seo Ye Rang]

233
00:13:45,388 --> 00:13:47,457
"CEO Seo Ye Rang?"

234
00:13:47,457 --> 00:13:51,606
That's the least romantic contact name ever.

235
00:13:58,653 --> 00:14:00,801
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable...</i>

236
00:14:00,801 --> 00:14:03,638
Why isn't she picking up?

237
00:14:03,638 --> 00:14:07,471
Don't tell me I screwed up again.

238
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:09,604
You probably did.

239
00:14:10,197 --> 00:14:11,917
Yeah, probably.

240
00:14:12,653 --> 00:14:14,297
Man, this sucks.

241
00:14:14,297 --> 00:14:17,298
It was nine years ago.
I can't even get mad about it now.

242
00:14:19,062 --> 00:14:21,162
Whatever.

243
00:14:21,162 --> 00:14:22,965
I'll sort things out with her.

244
00:14:22,965 --> 00:14:26,352
She'll come around soon.

245
00:14:26,352 --> 00:14:28,010
Look at this.

246
00:14:30,611 --> 00:14:32,271
What's this?

247
00:14:32,956 --> 00:14:36,512
"Jung Woo Jae, Director Yang Jun Mo's Muse?"

248
00:14:38,182 --> 00:14:40,152
What's with these two now?

249
00:14:40,152 --> 00:14:41,606
How did this happen?

250
00:14:41,606 --> 00:14:44,350
We don't even have the camcorder anymore.

251
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:46,816
So why are Woo Jae and Jun Mo...

252
00:14:47,558 --> 00:14:49,151
Yeah...

253
00:14:53,533 --> 00:14:56,149
When things get complicated, keep it simple.

254
00:14:56,149 --> 00:14:57,427
What?

255
00:14:58,023 --> 00:15:01,192
This is basically our happy ending, right?

256
00:15:01,873 --> 00:15:05,279
Aside from Ye Rang being pissed at me.

257
00:15:05,895 --> 00:15:07,655
Well...

258
00:15:07,655 --> 00:15:08,674
I guess.

259
00:15:08,674 --> 00:15:10,698
If nothing else happens.

260
00:15:10,698 --> 00:15:14,252
We just have to deal with
Yang Jun Mo and Park Gi Tae.

261
00:15:14,252 --> 00:15:16,282
Oh, how?

262
00:15:16,282 --> 00:15:19,545
Guess we should start figuring that out.

263
00:15:19,545 --> 00:15:21,079
Seriously...

264
00:15:45,404 --> 00:15:47,153
Did you get some rest?

265
00:15:47,787 --> 00:15:50,021
Oh, yeah.

266
00:15:50,021 --> 00:15:51,098
Are we heading back?

267
00:15:51,098 --> 00:15:52,256
We still have a little time.

268
00:15:52,256 --> 00:15:53,908
They're setting up the lights.

269
00:15:53,908 --> 00:15:55,161
Okay.

270
00:15:56,921 --> 00:15:58,967
About Ha Na today...

271
00:16:00,248 --> 00:16:02,261
Didn't she seem a little off?

272
00:16:05,155 --> 00:16:06,632
Really?

273
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,472
I didn't notice anything.

274
00:16:08,472 --> 00:16:09,851
Yeah?

275
00:16:16,659 --> 00:16:18,025
Why?

276
00:16:20,607 --> 00:16:22,939
Never mind. Get some rest.

277
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:40,913
"Eun Soo falls asleep on the couch
while watching a movie."

278
00:16:41,697 --> 00:16:44,414
She really fell asleep?

279
00:16:44,414 --> 00:16:48,200
The script changed.

280
00:17:21,635 --> 00:17:23,432
<i>Eun Soo...</i>

281
00:17:23,432 --> 00:17:26,505
<i>It's time for you to go back where you belong.</i>

282
00:17:26,505 --> 00:17:28,611
<i>I'll keep the past safe.</i>

283
00:17:29,256 --> 00:17:31,020
<i>In the future...</i>

284
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:33,453
<i>don't give anything up.</i>

285
00:17:34,942 --> 00:17:37,154
<i>Keep chasing your dreams.</i>

286
00:17:48,986 --> 00:17:51,823
Do you think it really was Woo Jae?

287
00:17:51,823 --> 00:17:52,920
I don't know...

288
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:55,661
We have a month until the final shoot.

289
00:17:56,294 --> 00:17:57,326
Yeah.

290
00:17:57,326 --> 00:18:00,047
And we can't go back to the past anymore.

291
00:18:00,047 --> 00:18:01,254
Right.

292
00:18:03,538 --> 00:18:05,785
You know what that means, right?

293
00:18:09,623 --> 00:18:12,401
It means something?

294
00:18:12,401 --> 00:18:17,005
Everything we do from now on is permanent.

295
00:18:19,352 --> 00:18:21,851
Oh, got it.

296
00:18:21,851 --> 00:18:24,021
You, me,

297
00:18:24,021 --> 00:18:25,446
and Woo Jae...

298
00:18:25,446 --> 00:18:27,285
We all need to be careful.

299
00:18:27,966 --> 00:18:29,272
Okay.

300
00:18:32,473 --> 00:18:34,216
<i>Miss you.</i>

301
00:18:34,216 --> 00:18:35,896
<i>What time should I come over tomorrow?</i>

302
00:18:35,896 --> 00:18:37,492
What is it?

303
00:18:37,492 --> 00:18:38,534
Why?

304
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:41,243
Woo Jae's coming over.

305
00:18:41,243 --> 00:18:42,774
So?

306
00:18:43,573 --> 00:18:45,848
A date at my place.

307
00:18:47,193 --> 00:18:48,959
Darn it.

308
00:18:50,192 --> 00:18:51,965
Beats me.

309
00:19:22,901 --> 00:19:24,467
Come in.

310
00:19:50,107 --> 00:19:52,231
You're good at everything, Kkomi.

311
00:19:52,231 --> 00:19:53,551
You make great coffee too.

312
00:19:53,551 --> 00:19:55,304
You could be a barista.

313
00:19:55,915 --> 00:19:58,385
Really? It's that good?

314
00:19:58,385 --> 00:20:00,672
Want me to start looking at places tomorrow?

315
00:20:00,672 --> 00:20:02,029
I could open you a cafe.

316
00:20:02,029 --> 00:20:04,162
A cafe?

317
00:20:04,162 --> 00:20:07,349
Thanks, but my day job keeps me busy enough.

318
00:20:07,349 --> 00:20:08,802
Right.

319
00:20:10,002 --> 00:20:11,559
But...

320
00:20:11,559 --> 00:20:14,625
Why do you call me Kkomi again?

321
00:20:21,031 --> 00:20:22,528
Because you're my little one.

322
00:20:22,528 --> 00:20:23,900
That's where "Kkomi" comes from.

323
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:25,934
<i>Oh my, Jung Woo Jae...</i>

324
00:20:25,934 --> 00:20:30,584
<i>You even came up with
a nickname as cute as you.</i>

325
00:20:33,775 --> 00:20:37,135
So... now that we're caffeinated...

326
00:20:37,925 --> 00:20:40,978
Ready to get started?

327
00:20:40,978 --> 00:20:43,815
"Get started?"

328
00:20:44,968 --> 00:20:46,659
<i>Jung Woo Jae...</i>

329
00:20:46,659 --> 00:20:50,372
<i>When did you get this bold?</i>

330
00:20:50,372 --> 00:20:52,281
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

331
00:21:02,521 --> 00:21:03,752
The script?

332
00:21:03,752 --> 00:21:06,597
Yeah. We said we'd rehearse together.

333
00:21:10,065 --> 00:21:11,982
We can start with this line.

334
00:21:12,684 --> 00:21:14,737
- Here.
- Okay.

335
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:18,053
All right.

336
00:21:20,844 --> 00:21:24,235
[Chef Yoon Ha Ru &amp; Nurungji Milk Cream Brûlée]
It's been way too long!

337
00:21:24,235 --> 00:21:25,744
Ye Rang hasn't changed a bit either.

338
00:21:25,744 --> 00:21:29,074
Chef Yoon, star quality
really runs in your family.

339
00:21:29,074 --> 00:21:31,573
Seriously, how do you look this good on camera?

340
00:21:31,573 --> 00:21:33,117
Oh, please.

341
00:21:33,117 --> 00:21:36,577
I hear you're directing every commercial
in Korea these days.

342
00:21:36,577 --> 00:21:39,167
Everyone's talking about you.

343
00:21:39,167 --> 00:21:40,927
How'd you hear about that?

344
00:21:40,927 --> 00:21:44,505
You've got a good eye, Seo Ye Rang.

345
00:21:44,505 --> 00:21:45,891
Of course I do.

346
00:21:45,891 --> 00:21:49,290
Just trust me and follow my lead
on this one too.

347
00:21:50,204 --> 00:21:53,834
Oh, there she is!

348
00:21:53,834 --> 00:21:56,888
This is CEO Seo Ye Rang.

349
00:21:56,888 --> 00:21:58,405
And here's our star.

350
00:21:58,405 --> 00:22:00,461
I like your style.

351
00:22:03,634 --> 00:22:09,041
Looks like we have similar taste.
I think we'll get along.

352
00:22:10,014 --> 00:22:13,465
Director Choi, I loved the storyboard.

353
00:22:13,465 --> 00:22:15,691
My work usually has that effect.

354
00:22:15,691 --> 00:22:20,413
But maybe I cast the wrong model.

355
00:22:21,133 --> 00:22:26,008
I can't take my eyes off Chef Yoon
long enough to notice the product.

356
00:22:26,008 --> 00:22:27,627
Is it just me?

357
00:22:30,398 --> 00:22:31,768
Oh, right.

358
00:22:31,768 --> 00:22:33,708
Do you know Pierre Moreau?

359
00:22:33,708 --> 00:22:35,488
Of course.

360
00:22:35,488 --> 00:22:38,042
He's huge in French cuisine.

361
00:22:38,042 --> 00:22:40,818
He's doing a secret pop-up in Korea.

362
00:22:40,818 --> 00:22:44,686
I managed to get two seats.

363
00:22:44,686 --> 00:22:45,698
Oh, really?

364
00:22:45,698 --> 00:22:47,528
I'd love that. Thank you.

365
00:22:47,528 --> 00:22:49,763
So, shall we start the meeting?

366
00:22:49,763 --> 00:22:51,364
Right this way.

367
00:22:53,924 --> 00:22:56,772
"I'm not letting you give up anything else."

368
00:22:57,398 --> 00:23:00,478
"From now on, I'll protect you. Eun Soo."

369
00:23:03,817 --> 00:23:06,425
- Want to take a break?
- Yeah.

370
00:23:06,425 --> 00:23:08,340
Want something to drink?

371
00:23:19,403 --> 00:23:21,065
What is it?

372
00:23:21,790 --> 00:23:23,028
Ha Na...

373
00:23:23,028 --> 00:23:24,963
I was just wondering...

374
00:23:24,963 --> 00:23:26,229
Yeah?

375
00:23:29,216 --> 00:23:30,656
Never mind.

376
00:23:34,703 --> 00:23:36,956
I missed you so much.

377
00:23:40,245 --> 00:23:41,630
What?

378
00:23:41,630 --> 00:23:44,109
We've been together all day.

379
00:23:44,109 --> 00:23:47,148
And we see each other almost every day on set.

380
00:23:47,755 --> 00:23:51,090
That's totally different.

381
00:24:23,829 --> 00:24:27,967
Can I sleep here tonight?

382
00:24:31,073 --> 00:24:32,523
Yeah.

383
00:24:32,523 --> 00:24:34,123
Stay.

384
00:24:34,922 --> 00:24:36,921
I want to be with you.

385
00:25:00,417 --> 00:25:03,682
A fresh twist on a familiar nutty flavor!

386
00:25:03,682 --> 00:25:06,507
On Daily with Chef Yoon Ha Ru!

387
00:25:06,507 --> 00:25:08,915
That concludes the presentation.

388
00:25:10,510 --> 00:25:11,860
Did you like it?

389
00:25:11,860 --> 00:25:13,497
Okay? Okay?

390
00:25:13,497 --> 00:25:14,640
Okay!

391
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,162
One more round of applause!

392
00:25:17,283 --> 00:25:19,682
Let's move on to the next meeting.

393
00:25:23,315 --> 00:25:24,742
Let's go.

394
00:25:25,958 --> 00:25:27,428
See you again soon.

395
00:25:27,428 --> 00:25:29,132
- I'll be in touch.
- Okay.

396
00:25:29,132 --> 00:25:30,734
Have a safe trip.

397
00:25:32,344 --> 00:25:34,271
I'll call you later.

398
00:25:34,271 --> 00:25:35,624
Ma'am...

399
00:25:37,835 --> 00:25:38,956
Good work.

400
00:25:38,956 --> 00:25:40,845
Oh, wait.

401
00:25:41,638 --> 00:25:44,188
Aren't we getting dinner?

402
00:25:44,188 --> 00:25:47,294
I worked hard today.
You're not even buying me something good?

403
00:25:48,590 --> 00:25:50,466
- Director Pyo.
- Yes.

404
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:52,559
You have the company card I gave you, right?

405
00:25:52,559 --> 00:25:56,806
Use it to get Chef Yoon something nice to eat.

406
00:25:56,806 --> 00:25:58,278
Yes, ma'am!

407
00:25:58,873 --> 00:26:00,353
But...

408
00:26:00,353 --> 00:26:01,906
Oh, right.

409
00:26:03,741 --> 00:26:05,765
And your style today...

410
00:26:05,765 --> 00:26:07,765
Your worst look yet.

411
00:26:10,471 --> 00:26:12,111
Bye.

412
00:26:14,470 --> 00:26:16,041
Boss...

413
00:26:16,041 --> 00:26:18,584
You're really going this far?

414
00:26:21,882 --> 00:26:23,755
- Hey.
- Yes?

415
00:26:23,755 --> 00:26:26,278
We broke up nine years ago,

416
00:26:26,278 --> 00:26:30,448
and then she signed me
to her agency two years later.

417
00:26:30,448 --> 00:26:32,245
What do you think?

418
00:26:32,245 --> 00:26:33,671
Can't you tell?

419
00:26:33,671 --> 00:26:35,004
[Exclusive Management Agreement]

420
00:26:41,412 --> 00:26:45,263
<i>What is this?</i>

421
00:26:45,263 --> 00:26:47,775
<i>I didn't call you here to get your hopes up.</i>

422
00:26:47,775 --> 00:26:49,658
<i>I'm making you this offer</i>

423
00:26:49,658 --> 00:26:52,449
<i>because I see value and potential in you.</i>

424
00:26:52,449 --> 00:26:54,126
<i>You'll like the terms.</i>

425
00:26:54,126 --> 00:26:57,534
<i>If you don't have any special requests,
sign it.</i>

426
00:26:57,534 --> 00:26:59,853
CEO Seo's all business.

427
00:26:59,853 --> 00:27:02,646
But in the end,

428
00:27:02,646 --> 00:27:05,279
it worked out for both of you.

429
00:27:07,718 --> 00:27:09,981
Oh, right.

430
00:27:09,981 --> 00:27:12,889
Look at this.

431
00:27:12,889 --> 00:27:14,426
[CEO S in Secret Marriage Talks
with Heir to Top-10 Conglomerate]

432
00:27:14,426 --> 00:27:15,505
<i>I think...</i>

433
00:27:15,505 --> 00:27:18,336
<i>I'm going to like you even more, Ye Rang.</i>

434
00:27:18,336 --> 00:27:20,126
- What?
- Oh my...

435
00:27:20,126 --> 00:27:22,260
That bastard...

436
00:27:22,260 --> 00:27:25,473
He's the guy from the hotel cafe!

437
00:27:44,748 --> 00:27:48,721
<i>I'm never letting you go again.</i>

438
00:27:49,962 --> 00:27:54,056
<i>You're what romance means to me now.</i>

439
00:27:55,077 --> 00:27:57,014
<i>You know...</i>

440
00:27:57,014 --> 00:28:00,311
<i>I hope you live a happy life,</i>

441
00:28:00,311 --> 00:28:02,254
<i>and a long one at that.</i>

442
00:28:02,254 --> 00:28:05,831
<i>You're so cute.</i>

443
00:28:08,834 --> 00:28:10,484
<i>For me...</i>

444
00:28:10,484 --> 00:28:14,568
<i>the fact that I can love you
with everything I have...</i>

445
00:28:14,568 --> 00:28:16,640
<i>just gives me so much joy.</i>

446
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:18,467
<i>It makes me happy.</i>

447
00:28:36,913 --> 00:28:38,836
I know everything now.

448
00:28:39,441 --> 00:28:41,684
You went back to the past to save me,

449
00:28:41,684 --> 00:28:44,418
and gave up the things
that mattered most to you.

450
00:28:44,418 --> 00:28:46,088
You can stop now.

451
00:28:46,088 --> 00:28:48,381
I did it because I wanted to.

452
00:28:54,064 --> 00:28:58,729
Now I'm going to do what I want.

453
00:29:00,152 --> 00:29:04,416
I'm not letting you give up anything else.

454
00:29:04,416 --> 00:29:07,809
From now on, I'll protect you. Eun Soo.

455
00:29:11,140 --> 00:29:12,396
Cut! Okay.

456
00:29:12,396 --> 00:29:14,104
Okay!

457
00:29:20,738 --> 00:29:22,931
- And this time...
- Got it.

458
00:29:32,928 --> 00:29:35,465
Hello, sir.

459
00:29:35,465 --> 00:29:37,765
Oh, what brings you here?

460
00:29:37,765 --> 00:29:39,295
Well...

461
00:29:39,295 --> 00:29:41,721
My sister's here... and a friend too.

462
00:29:41,721 --> 00:29:43,961
Figured I'd stop by.

463
00:29:45,422 --> 00:29:46,688
Yeah.

464
00:29:47,289 --> 00:29:49,971
Sir. About that prop you mentioned...

465
00:29:49,971 --> 00:29:52,498
It should be ready soon.

466
00:29:54,965 --> 00:29:56,595
- Seok Min.
- Yes?

467
00:29:56,595 --> 00:29:58,495
I'm going to get some air.

468
00:29:58,495 --> 00:30:00,114
Okay.

469
00:30:00,114 --> 00:30:01,701
Darn it.

470
00:30:10,769 --> 00:30:12,270
Seo Ye Rang.

471
00:30:23,467 --> 00:30:24,784
What is it?

472
00:30:24,784 --> 00:30:26,335
You have something to say?

473
00:30:26,935 --> 00:30:28,853
Yeah, I do.

474
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:33,652
I saw the rumor.

475
00:30:34,794 --> 00:30:36,397
It's not true, right?

476
00:30:36,397 --> 00:30:37,994
You wouldn't do that.

477
00:30:37,994 --> 00:30:39,353
Right?

478
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,655
You really...

479
00:30:44,261 --> 00:30:47,913
You don't love me anymore?

480
00:30:49,126 --> 00:30:50,857
Do you think I'm a joke?

481
00:30:50,857 --> 00:30:52,106
What?

482
00:30:53,186 --> 00:30:55,663
How did you even get there?

483
00:30:55,663 --> 00:30:57,613
Do I still look like that pathetic girl

484
00:30:57,613 --> 00:31:00,906
who clung to you and...

485
00:31:00,906 --> 00:31:03,365
begged you to love me?

486
00:31:03,998 --> 00:31:06,346
- What are you...
- Enough.

487
00:31:06,935 --> 00:31:11,495
If you don't want to ruin what we have now,

488
00:31:11,495 --> 00:31:13,387
then at least show me...

489
00:31:14,094 --> 00:31:15,607
a little respect.

490
00:31:57,988 --> 00:31:59,694
[Yoon Ha Na]

491
00:32:02,775 --> 00:32:04,550
Hey, Oranges!

492
00:32:04,550 --> 00:32:06,990
Welcome to Cool Guy's Take. I'm Minu.

493
00:32:06,990 --> 00:32:09,481
We have a very special guest today.

494
00:32:09,481 --> 00:32:11,128
Star of The Chef Show

495
00:32:11,128 --> 00:32:13,039
and winner of Chef Wars!

496
00:32:13,039 --> 00:32:14,165
<i>If you...</i>

497
00:32:14,165 --> 00:32:16,794
<i>don't want to ruin what we have now,</i>

498
00:32:16,794 --> 00:32:19,271
<i>then at least show me a little respect.</i>

499
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:22,128
Chef Yoon Ha Ru!

500
00:32:22,128 --> 00:32:23,868
Great to have you here.

501
00:32:24,725 --> 00:32:26,919
Chef?

502
00:32:29,538 --> 00:32:30,691
Yes?

503
00:32:31,611 --> 00:32:33,731
Oh, sorry.

504
00:32:34,584 --> 00:32:37,508
You seem pretty nervous.

505
00:32:37,508 --> 00:32:41,586
Why don't we loosen up with our first story?

506
00:32:41,586 --> 00:32:42,866
Sure!

507
00:32:44,951 --> 00:32:48,128
This one's from "Hopeless Romantic,"
an office worker in her early 30s.

508
00:32:48,128 --> 00:32:50,152
"I dated my ex for four years in my 20s.

509
00:32:50,152 --> 00:32:54,613
We broke up three years ago,
but I still can't get over him.

510
00:32:55,414 --> 00:32:58,061
<i>My ex was everything to me in my 20s.</i>

511
00:32:58,061 --> 00:33:02,657
<i>But he started putting his career
and success first.</i>

512
00:33:02,657 --> 00:33:04,127
<i>Before I knew it,</i>

513
00:33:04,127 --> 00:33:06,195
<i>I was the only one still holding on...</i>

514
00:33:06,195 --> 00:33:08,487
<i>practically begging him to love me."</i>

515
00:33:08,487 --> 00:33:10,240
<i>Do I still look like that pathetic girl...</i>

516
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:12,914
<i>who clung to you and...</i>

517
00:33:12,914 --> 00:33:15,327
<i>begged you to love me?</i>

518
00:33:15,327 --> 00:33:17,604
<i>"In the end, I broke up with him.</i>

519
00:33:17,604 --> 00:33:19,224
<i>It's been three years now.</i>

520
00:33:19,224 --> 00:33:22,561
<i>So why can't I stop thinking about him?"</i>

521
00:33:22,561 --> 00:33:23,885
All right.

522
00:33:23,885 --> 00:33:27,695
What advice would you give
our "Hopeless Romantic?"

523
00:33:35,724 --> 00:33:38,290
"Hopeless Romantic."

524
00:33:40,007 --> 00:33:42,110
That guy's...

525
00:33:42,797 --> 00:33:47,998
probably living with regret right now.

526
00:33:49,613 --> 00:33:51,526
I know exactly how he feels.

527
00:33:52,294 --> 00:33:54,324
I've been there.

528
00:33:56,321 --> 00:33:58,934
We broke up nine years ago.

529
00:34:01,694 --> 00:34:03,467
I still...

530
00:34:04,261 --> 00:34:07,936
I still love her.

531
00:34:08,780 --> 00:34:12,018
<i>Is this a public confession?</i>

532
00:34:12,018 --> 00:34:13,575
<i>"A public confession?"</i>

533
00:34:14,705 --> 00:34:17,319
I guess it is.

534
00:34:18,365 --> 00:34:21,563
Let's call it that.

535
00:34:25,091 --> 00:34:28,488
My biggest regret in life...

536
00:34:28,488 --> 00:34:32,248
<i>is that I was so busy chasing success,</i>

537
00:34:32,248 --> 00:34:37,302
<i>I never realized how lonely she was.</i>

538
00:34:37,302 --> 00:34:41,475
If I ever get another chance with her...

539
00:34:43,107 --> 00:34:48,444
I'll devote every day I have to her.

540
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:51,176
<i>I loved her then...</i>

541
00:34:51,176 --> 00:34:57,756
and I still love her very much.

542
00:35:00,065 --> 00:35:02,755
<i>A confession nine years later!</i>

543
00:35:02,755 --> 00:35:06,563
<i>Do you think she's listening right now?</i>

544
00:35:06,563 --> 00:35:10,305
- You bastard...
<i>- I hope things work out for both</i>

545
00:35:10,305 --> 00:35:12,237
<i>"Hopeless Romantic" and Chef Ha Ru.</i>

546
00:35:12,237 --> 00:35:14,759
<i>Let's move on to our next story.</i>

547
00:35:17,652 --> 00:35:19,118
[Kang Do Hoon]

548
00:35:37,710 --> 00:35:39,936
I heard your show earlier.

549
00:35:40,950 --> 00:35:42,420
You okay?

550
00:35:42,420 --> 00:35:44,179
Of course.

551
00:35:45,330 --> 00:35:48,827
Once I take care of everything,
I'll win Boss's heart back.

552
00:35:48,827 --> 00:35:50,275
Don't worry.

553
00:35:50,275 --> 00:35:51,976
You know who I am.

554
00:35:56,370 --> 00:35:58,316
Ugh, my head...

555
00:35:58,990 --> 00:36:00,100
When are they getting here?

556
00:36:00,100 --> 00:36:02,527
- What?
- I'm just asking...

557
00:36:02,527 --> 00:36:04,744
- They said they're almost here.
- Yeah, but when?

558
00:36:04,744 --> 00:36:07,235
I just told you, they're almost here.

559
00:36:07,235 --> 00:36:09,174
Why are you getting mad?

560
00:36:09,174 --> 00:36:11,798
You got mad first.

561
00:36:11,798 --> 00:36:13,924
I just asked when they'd be here.

562
00:36:13,924 --> 00:36:16,339
- And I said they're almost here...
- Be quiet.

563
00:36:16,339 --> 00:36:18,038
- You started...
- Knock it off!

564
00:36:18,038 --> 00:36:20,188
Hey! Hands off!

565
00:36:22,233 --> 00:36:23,930
What's wrong with you?

566
00:36:23,930 --> 00:36:27,067
These people are trustworthy, right?

567
00:36:27,067 --> 00:36:29,053
Yeah, that's what I heard.

568
00:36:29,053 --> 00:36:33,213
They say this company only hires
seasoned industry veterans.

569
00:36:33,213 --> 00:36:34,820
They're the real deal.

570
00:36:34,820 --> 00:36:36,219
Don't worry.

571
00:36:48,416 --> 00:36:50,573
I didn't want to come empty-handed.

572
00:36:50,573 --> 00:36:52,086
I thought these were pretty.

573
00:36:52,086 --> 00:36:54,437
Wow, thank you.

574
00:36:54,437 --> 00:36:56,391
Hello. I'm Cha Ah Ryeong,

575
00:36:56,391 --> 00:36:59,124
- CEO of OK Planning.
- Wait!

576
00:36:59,124 --> 00:37:01,488
With Ha Ri gone...

577
00:37:01,488 --> 00:37:03,188
- I'm the CEO.
- What? Didn't you hear?

578
00:37:03,188 --> 00:37:04,321
I'm the CEO.

579
00:37:04,321 --> 00:37:06,258
- That was a joke...
- No, I'm serious.

580
00:37:06,258 --> 00:37:09,241
- Sorry. Court ran late.
- I have business cards...

581
00:37:09,241 --> 00:37:10,610
Hello.

582
00:37:11,521 --> 00:37:13,609
- Dad?
- Dad?

583
00:37:13,609 --> 00:37:15,020
"Dad?"

584
00:37:16,639 --> 00:37:18,663
I'm not.

585
00:37:18,663 --> 00:37:20,349
I'm not!

586
00:37:21,033 --> 00:37:24,172
I'm single, actually...

587
00:37:25,042 --> 00:37:26,706
- I'm the CEO.
- No, you're not.

588
00:37:26,706 --> 00:37:28,117
Ha Ri told me I was.

589
00:37:28,117 --> 00:37:29,743
I already had business cards made.

590
00:37:29,743 --> 00:37:31,960
I'm the CEO until Ha Ri comes back.

591
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:32,863
Mr. Gwak...

592
00:37:32,863 --> 00:37:35,040
- What? Hey...
- Enough!

593
00:37:35,040 --> 00:37:37,287
You're all too loud. Just go sit down.

594
00:37:37,966 --> 00:37:39,213
- Let's have a seat.
- Yeah...

595
00:37:39,213 --> 00:37:41,766
- Okay.
- Who cares who's CEO anyway...

596
00:37:41,766 --> 00:37:44,281
- Wait, were you married?
- I told you, no.

597
00:37:44,872 --> 00:37:47,058
Stop staring. I'm not your dad.

598
00:37:47,058 --> 00:37:48,444
Dad...

599
00:37:51,730 --> 00:37:55,682
So our clients are pretty famous, huh?

600
00:37:57,001 --> 00:37:58,365
Oh, well...

601
00:37:58,365 --> 00:38:01,651
We're not here for autographs. Relax.

602
00:38:01,651 --> 00:38:04,828
Confidentiality always comes first.

603
00:38:04,828 --> 00:38:06,552
- Okay?
- Okay.

604
00:38:06,552 --> 00:38:09,512
Okay. Shall we get started?

605
00:38:09,512 --> 00:38:10,742
Yes.

606
00:38:25,042 --> 00:38:27,691
[Lost Time, Crank Up D-25]

607
00:38:28,558 --> 00:38:30,656
Let me guess...

608
00:38:31,414 --> 00:38:33,871
Yoon Ha Na's birthday?

609
00:38:33,871 --> 00:38:35,524
So...

610
00:38:36,218 --> 00:38:37,816
It's my birthday.

611
00:38:37,816 --> 00:38:41,394
1-9-9-3-0-5-0-7.

612
00:38:44,303 --> 00:38:47,070
Knew it.

613
00:38:47,856 --> 00:38:49,343
Let's go in.

614
00:38:51,514 --> 00:38:53,300
What's all that?

615
00:39:09,910 --> 00:39:12,465
This is really sensitive...

616
00:39:14,143 --> 00:39:15,615
Just stay seated.

617
00:39:15,615 --> 00:39:16,835
I was just curious.

618
00:39:16,835 --> 00:39:20,161
I'm allergic to men.

619
00:39:41,472 --> 00:39:42,976
I knew it...

620
00:39:42,976 --> 00:39:44,923
Darn it!

621
00:39:46,212 --> 00:39:48,595
What do you have against me?

622
00:39:48,595 --> 00:39:50,730
I was just curious.

623
00:39:50,730 --> 00:39:53,759
I told you to stay seated. I'll handle it.

624
00:39:55,501 --> 00:39:57,387
I told you, I'm allergic.

625
00:40:09,290 --> 00:40:11,434
I searched everything, down to the underwear.

626
00:40:11,434 --> 00:40:13,383
This is all I found.

627
00:40:13,383 --> 00:40:15,066
These guys are professionals.

628
00:40:15,066 --> 00:40:17,579
They hid these really well.

629
00:40:17,579 --> 00:40:20,326
So there shouldn't be anything left, right?

630
00:40:20,326 --> 00:40:22,350
Don't worry.

631
00:40:22,350 --> 00:40:24,453
This is what we do...

632
00:40:25,867 --> 00:40:28,317
What's your problem?

633
00:40:28,317 --> 00:40:29,919
No, I...

634
00:40:30,903 --> 00:40:33,283
I was just curious.

635
00:40:33,996 --> 00:40:35,756
I'm done.

636
00:40:37,145 --> 00:40:38,995
I'll stay back.

637
00:40:45,434 --> 00:40:48,092
<i>Woo Jae's place and car are clear.</i>

638
00:40:48,092 --> 00:40:50,078
Okay.

639
00:40:50,078 --> 00:40:52,066
Ha Na, they're ready to shoot.

640
00:40:52,066 --> 00:40:54,074
- Okay.
- Let's go.

641
00:40:56,673 --> 00:40:58,986
- Good work.
- Good work!

642
00:40:58,986 --> 00:41:00,670
Want to grab a bite together?

643
00:41:00,670 --> 00:41:03,066
- I'd love that!
- Sure.

644
00:41:03,066 --> 00:41:04,753
Actually...

645
00:41:04,753 --> 00:41:07,217
I already have plans.

646
00:41:07,217 --> 00:41:08,925
You do?

647
00:41:08,925 --> 00:41:11,101
What plans?

648
00:41:11,101 --> 00:41:12,885
I'll tell you later.

649
00:41:12,885 --> 00:41:14,892
- I'll call you.
- Okay.

650
00:41:14,892 --> 00:41:15,954
Seok Min, let's go.

651
00:41:15,954 --> 00:41:17,958
- See you.
- Yeah.

652
00:41:17,958 --> 00:41:19,918
Okay, Ha Na.

653
00:41:19,918 --> 00:41:21,371
I'll call you.

654
00:41:27,711 --> 00:41:30,501
I talked to Ye Rang about the stalking.

655
00:41:30,501 --> 00:41:32,341
Yeah? What did she say?

656
00:41:32,341 --> 00:41:33,551
<i>Stalking?</i>

657
00:41:33,551 --> 00:41:34,952
<i>What stalking?</i>

658
00:41:34,952 --> 00:41:37,572
<i>Ha Na, you had a stalker?</i>

659
00:41:37,572 --> 00:41:38,656
<i>Since when?</i>

660
00:41:38,656 --> 00:41:40,416
<i>No, it's nothing.</i>

661
00:41:40,416 --> 00:41:41,910
<i>I'll let you go.</i>

662
00:41:41,910 --> 00:41:43,286
2017.

663
00:41:43,286 --> 00:41:45,419
That was the first and last time.

664
00:41:45,419 --> 00:41:46,983
There was nothing after that.

665
00:41:46,983 --> 00:41:50,665
So all that persistent stalking just stopped?

666
00:41:51,528 --> 00:41:53,085
What does that mean?

667
00:41:53,085 --> 00:41:55,390
Is that a good thing?

668
00:41:55,390 --> 00:41:57,392
I don't know.

669
00:41:57,392 --> 00:42:00,166
I'm not sure it works in our favor.

670
00:42:01,006 --> 00:42:05,386
But someone still bugged the place
and tracked your location.

671
00:42:05,386 --> 00:42:07,101
So what the hell is going on?

672
00:42:07,688 --> 00:42:09,543
What about Park Gi Tae?

673
00:42:09,543 --> 00:42:11,233
What did Hyeong Won say?

674
00:42:12,420 --> 00:42:13,657
He said...

675
00:42:13,657 --> 00:42:16,117
<i>Did you look into him?</i>

676
00:42:16,117 --> 00:42:19,783
<i>No one from the orphanage
knows anything either.</i>

677
00:42:21,534 --> 00:42:24,197
<i>Even the police couldn't find him.
How could we?</i>

678
00:42:24,197 --> 00:42:26,139
<i>But that was ten years ago.</i>

679
00:42:26,139 --> 00:42:28,163
<i>Why are you asking about him now?</i>

680
00:42:28,163 --> 00:42:29,958
<i>Did something happen?</i>

681
00:42:29,958 --> 00:42:32,996
He doesn't know much either.

682
00:42:38,153 --> 00:42:41,896
Park Gi Tae's registration
was canceled five years ago.

683
00:42:41,896 --> 00:42:44,447
He's been living under stolen identities,

684
00:42:44,447 --> 00:42:46,726
changing names every so often.

685
00:42:46,726 --> 00:42:48,049
This isn't going to be easy.

686
00:42:48,049 --> 00:42:49,176
Ha Na.

687
00:42:49,176 --> 00:42:51,260
I'll do everything I can for you.

688
00:42:51,260 --> 00:42:52,843
Oh, thank you.

689
00:42:52,843 --> 00:42:56,688
Ha Na, I'll work even harder than he will.

690
00:42:56,688 --> 00:42:59,355
- Okay...
- Ha Na, I...

691
00:43:00,539 --> 00:43:02,296
Who is it?

692
00:43:02,296 --> 00:43:04,506
Were you expecting anyone?

693
00:43:04,506 --> 00:43:05,943
No.

694
00:43:07,306 --> 00:43:08,866
No way...

695
00:43:14,196 --> 00:43:16,934
Oh, an actor.

696
00:43:39,106 --> 00:43:40,961
[Fourth Jump: Returns to 2026
during Woo Jae and Hyeong Won's fight]

697
00:44:17,989 --> 00:44:20,247
[If we fall into the water with that,
we jump to the time of the recorded footage]

698
00:44:23,337 --> 00:44:26,733
So, just like it says here,
you two traveled through time...

699
00:44:26,733 --> 00:44:30,969
and every time you did,
you two switched bodies.

700
00:44:38,704 --> 00:44:40,294
<i>Woo Jae.</i>

701
00:44:43,950 --> 00:44:45,821
<i>You crazy bastard, Jung Woo Jae!</i>

702
00:44:45,821 --> 00:44:47,238
<i>You bastard...</i>

703
00:44:47,238 --> 00:44:49,178
<i>What took you so long?</i>

704
00:44:49,178 --> 00:44:51,414
<i>Don't ever come looking for me...</i>

705
00:44:52,198 --> 00:44:54,051
<i>You bastard.</i>

706
00:44:55,824 --> 00:44:58,498
<i>We're running out of time.</i>

707
00:44:58,498 --> 00:45:00,075
<i>You can't get hurt.</i>

708
00:45:00,075 --> 00:45:02,504
<i>You can't get sick either.</i>

709
00:45:02,504 --> 00:45:04,528
<i>Don't protect anyone else.</i>

710
00:45:04,528 --> 00:45:06,915
<i>Just protect yourself, okay?</i>

711
00:45:06,915 --> 00:45:08,632
<i>For me...</i>

712
00:45:09,351 --> 00:45:13,125
<i>the fact that I can love you
with everything I have...</i>

713
00:45:13,125 --> 00:45:15,031
<i>just gives me so much joy.</i>

714
00:45:16,403 --> 00:45:18,093
<i>It makes me happy.</i>

715
00:45:18,093 --> 00:45:21,881
And not long ago,
you came back from the past again.

716
00:45:21,881 --> 00:45:24,965
You two did all this to save me.

717
00:45:25,580 --> 00:45:26,894
Right?

718
00:45:29,921 --> 00:45:31,361
Yeah.

719
00:45:37,697 --> 00:45:39,001
Yeah.

720
00:45:39,001 --> 00:45:41,073
Maybe this is for the best.

721
00:45:42,361 --> 00:45:45,264
Now that everything's out in the open,
I can finally ask.

722
00:45:45,264 --> 00:45:46,930
What's your deal?

723
00:45:47,883 --> 00:45:52,341
- What?
- How'd you end up teaming up with Jun Mo?

724
00:45:52,341 --> 00:45:54,125
What was it again?

725
00:45:54,125 --> 00:45:56,698
Mu... music? Or something?

726
00:45:56,698 --> 00:45:57,722
Muse.

727
00:45:57,722 --> 00:45:59,448
Yeah, that.

728
00:46:00,045 --> 00:46:02,108
How did that happen?

729
00:46:09,272 --> 00:46:10,901
<i>You and I...</i>

730
00:46:10,901 --> 00:46:13,737
<i>may be in different situations,
but we want the same thing.</i>

731
00:46:15,503 --> 00:46:17,155
<i>Keeping Ha Na safe.</i>

732
00:46:20,117 --> 00:46:22,496
<i>What do you want me to do?</i>

733
00:46:31,141 --> 00:46:33,280
<i>Bring me the camcorder.</i>

734
00:46:35,441 --> 00:46:37,362
<i>Can you do that?</i>

735
00:46:43,208 --> 00:46:45,208
<i>I have one condition.</i>

736
00:46:47,341 --> 00:46:49,601
<i>From now on,</i>

737
00:46:50,241 --> 00:46:51,697
<i>you make your films with me.</i>

738
00:46:51,697 --> 00:46:54,634
<i>If you want, I'll even do it for life.</i>

739
00:46:54,634 --> 00:46:56,178
<i>What?</i>

740
00:46:56,178 --> 00:46:59,579
<i>Whatever script you bring me,</i>

741
00:46:59,579 --> 00:47:01,936
<i>you won't have to worry
about production or financing.</i>

742
00:47:01,936 --> 00:47:04,607
<i>I'll make sure it gets a theatrical release.</i>

743
00:47:05,375 --> 00:47:08,631
<i>You see the deal, right?</i>

744
00:47:09,893 --> 00:47:11,205
<i>But...</i>

745
00:47:11,205 --> 00:47:13,228
<i>From this moment on,</i>

746
00:47:13,228 --> 00:47:15,802
<i>stay away from Ha Na.</i>

747
00:47:15,802 --> 00:47:17,581
<i>Whatever it is.</i>

748
00:47:22,061 --> 00:47:23,218
<i>Okay.</i>

749
00:47:23,218 --> 00:47:25,145
<i>And one more condition.</i>

750
00:47:25,145 --> 00:47:27,031
<i>One film.</i>

751
00:47:27,644 --> 00:47:29,976
<i>You have to do one film with Ha Na.</i>

752
00:47:29,976 --> 00:47:31,922
<i>The two of you as the leads.</i>

753
00:47:33,475 --> 00:47:37,508
<i>I've got a story in mind for both of you.</i>

754
00:47:37,508 --> 00:47:40,680
<i>And with you right there beside her,</i>

755
00:47:40,680 --> 00:47:42,501
<i>what could I possibly do?</i>

756
00:47:43,111 --> 00:47:44,475
<i>Right?</i>

757
00:47:52,678 --> 00:47:54,964
So that's why...

758
00:47:54,964 --> 00:47:58,488
the stalking stopped.

759
00:48:01,546 --> 00:48:03,546
I'm sorry, Woo Jae.

760
00:48:04,339 --> 00:48:05,629
Why are you sorry?

761
00:48:05,629 --> 00:48:07,715
I'm the reason any of this happened.

762
00:48:16,993 --> 00:48:20,871
We're actually doing pretty great now.

763
00:48:20,871 --> 00:48:22,835
You're alive and well.

764
00:48:22,835 --> 00:48:27,512
And Ha Na and I have pretty good lives too.

765
00:48:27,512 --> 00:48:29,536
We're in a good place.

766
00:48:29,536 --> 00:48:33,817
So lighten up, okay?

767
00:48:38,280 --> 00:48:41,793
Ha Ru, you can't do judo anymore.

768
00:48:41,793 --> 00:48:45,153
Ha Na, you lost the career
you worked so hard for...

769
00:48:45,153 --> 00:48:47,519
and I got to keep everything.

770
00:48:48,800 --> 00:48:50,874
Hey. I told you.

771
00:48:50,874 --> 00:48:54,860
I did enough judo. More than enough.

772
00:48:56,362 --> 00:48:57,526
Same here!

773
00:48:57,526 --> 00:49:01,179
So what about my career? I'm a lead again now.

774
00:49:03,069 --> 00:49:07,988
But you kept going back, giving up so much...

775
00:49:07,988 --> 00:49:10,454
That means the future never changed, right?

776
00:49:11,041 --> 00:49:13,005
Plus, those guys from earlier...

777
00:49:13,005 --> 00:49:16,652
Something's still not over, is it?

778
00:49:17,826 --> 00:49:20,550
- Well... that's because...
- Please.

779
00:49:20,550 --> 00:49:22,270
Just stop.

780
00:49:26,186 --> 00:49:31,314
Stop giving things up because of me.

781
00:49:32,196 --> 00:49:33,863
Please.

782
00:49:35,147 --> 00:49:37,147
You're unbelievable.

783
00:49:37,947 --> 00:49:39,197
Hey.

784
00:49:39,197 --> 00:49:42,583
After all this time with us,
you still don't know us?

785
00:49:42,583 --> 00:49:44,639
You think you can look at us like that...

786
00:49:44,639 --> 00:49:46,195
and say, "Please?"

787
00:49:46,195 --> 00:49:50,296
And we'll just say, "Okay?"

788
00:49:52,016 --> 00:49:55,594
Just shut up and cooperate.

789
00:49:55,594 --> 00:49:58,359
Yoon Ha Na, you explain.

790
00:49:58,359 --> 00:50:01,017
Okay. Listen carefully.

791
00:51:00,172 --> 00:51:03,029
For now, all your schedules are on hold.

792
00:51:03,029 --> 00:51:05,933
Until this blows over,

793
00:51:05,933 --> 00:51:07,767
we just have to ride it out, Eun Soo.

794
00:51:07,767 --> 00:51:09,949
I'm sorry.

795
00:51:11,854 --> 00:51:15,377
I know those articles about Eun Soo
aren't true.

796
00:51:15,377 --> 00:51:18,227
You know Eun Soo better than anyone.

797
00:51:18,227 --> 00:51:20,663
The public doesn't care what's true.

798
00:51:20,663 --> 00:51:22,817
They just want someone to tear apart...

799
00:51:22,817 --> 00:51:25,256
Cut! Sorry.

800
00:51:25,256 --> 00:51:28,157
Let's give Eun Soo a little more contrast.

801
00:51:28,157 --> 00:51:29,767
We'll adjust the lighting.

802
00:51:29,767 --> 00:51:32,275
We'll touch up the makeup too.

803
00:51:40,055 --> 00:51:41,532
<i>No trace of any transfers.</i>

804
00:51:41,532 --> 00:51:43,745
<i>Looks like they only dealt in cash.</i>

805
00:51:43,745 --> 00:51:45,475
<i>They only used TeleTalk.</i>

806
00:51:45,475 --> 00:51:48,129
<i>Apparently, it's nearly impossible to hack.</i>

807
00:51:48,805 --> 00:51:50,295
Sir.

808
00:51:50,295 --> 00:51:53,089
Have those two gotten into stocks lately?

809
00:52:08,035 --> 00:52:10,134
Take a break now and then.

810
00:52:11,624 --> 00:52:13,083
Here.

811
00:52:18,917 --> 00:52:21,376
Tomorrow's finally the last shoot.

812
00:52:22,537 --> 00:52:24,014
Yeah.

813
00:52:24,014 --> 00:52:26,700
Don't you think it's a little too quiet?

814
00:52:26,700 --> 00:52:28,157
Yang Jun Mo?

815
00:52:28,157 --> 00:52:29,420
Yeah.

816
00:52:29,420 --> 00:52:32,447
We got rid of all the bugs
and tracking devices.

817
00:52:32,447 --> 00:52:34,980
So why hasn't he done anything?

818
00:52:34,980 --> 00:52:36,970
Maybe he's just busy wrapping up the movie.

819
00:52:36,970 --> 00:52:39,560
Being a director and all.

820
00:52:39,560 --> 00:52:41,510
It's been too quiet.

821
00:52:41,510 --> 00:52:43,813
Honestly, it makes me nervous.

822
00:52:45,964 --> 00:52:50,350
Let's just make sure
tomorrow's final shoot goes well.

823
00:52:50,350 --> 00:52:53,215
You used to work with Jun Mo a lot, right?

824
00:52:53,215 --> 00:52:55,101
You even won Best Actress.

825
00:52:55,101 --> 00:52:56,119
Well...

826
00:52:56,119 --> 00:53:00,547
I want you to get back
everything you gave up because of me.

827
00:53:01,355 --> 00:53:05,868
That's why I want to see this movie through.

828
00:53:07,253 --> 00:53:08,566
Yeah.

829
00:53:10,680 --> 00:53:12,083
Sorry.

830
00:53:12,083 --> 00:53:13,903
<i>Babe!</i>

831
00:53:13,903 --> 00:53:15,573
<i>Oh my.</i>

832
00:53:15,573 --> 00:53:17,496
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

833
00:53:18,336 --> 00:53:20,087
<i>What?</i>

834
00:53:20,087 --> 00:53:22,536
<i>You never get tired of me, do you?</i>

835
00:53:22,536 --> 00:53:23,930
<i>How could I?</i>

836
00:53:23,930 --> 00:53:26,508
<i>I fall for you all over again
every time I see you.</i>

837
00:53:26,508 --> 00:53:28,662
<i>Even after 14 years.</i>

838
00:53:30,236 --> 00:53:32,766
No. What are you sorry for?

839
00:53:32,766 --> 00:53:34,106
No...

840
00:53:34,106 --> 00:53:35,806
I'm so sorry.

841
00:53:44,558 --> 00:53:47,569
<i>If you can never be wholly mine,</i>

842
00:53:47,569 --> 00:53:49,786
<i>I'll stop time</i>

843
00:53:49,786 --> 00:53:54,940
<i>and lock you away
in the most perfect, eternal cage.</i>

844
00:53:54,940 --> 00:53:57,416
<i>My poor little ones...</i>

845
00:53:57,416 --> 00:53:59,446
<i>Do not grieve.</i>

846
00:53:59,446 --> 00:54:04,602
<i>I will lead you to true salvation.</i>

847
00:54:12,186 --> 00:54:14,530
Enjoy! Have some hot broth too!

848
00:54:14,530 --> 00:54:16,483
- Hello!
- Hi.

849
00:54:16,483 --> 00:54:17,507
I'll have tteokbokki.

850
00:54:17,507 --> 00:54:19,124
Lots of tteokbokki, please!

851
00:54:19,124 --> 00:54:20,984
Hello!

852
00:54:20,984 --> 00:54:23,014
- And some sundae, please.
- Sundae!

853
00:54:23,014 --> 00:54:24,487
One, two, three!

854
00:54:24,487 --> 00:54:27,486
Nice! One, two, three!

855
00:54:27,486 --> 00:54:30,757
You know this last scene won't be easy.

856
00:54:30,757 --> 00:54:32,780
It'll be tough,

857
00:54:32,780 --> 00:54:34,310
but this is the scene

858
00:54:34,310 --> 00:54:37,907
where your rawest, most beautiful
performances will live forever.

859
00:54:37,907 --> 00:54:39,350
Give it your all.

860
00:54:39,350 --> 00:54:41,606
- Yes.
- Okay.

861
00:54:41,606 --> 00:54:43,310
All right.

862
00:54:43,310 --> 00:54:45,310
Let's make it count.

863
00:54:47,258 --> 00:54:49,152
Woo Jae, Ha Na.

864
00:54:50,132 --> 00:54:52,645
- You've got this.
- Go for it!

865
00:54:54,604 --> 00:54:56,808
Final shoot for Lost Time.

866
00:54:56,808 --> 00:55:00,452
Day 52, Scene 121, Take 1!

867
00:55:02,054 --> 00:55:04,078
All right. Ready...

868
00:55:04,078 --> 00:55:05,211
Action!

869
00:55:05,848 --> 00:55:07,641
Yeong Hyeon.

870
00:55:10,347 --> 00:55:11,980
Oh, no...

871
00:55:16,063 --> 00:55:18,087
Eun Soo.

872
00:55:18,087 --> 00:55:19,676
I'm glad.

873
00:55:26,505 --> 00:55:28,819
Yeong Hyeon.

874
00:55:28,819 --> 00:55:31,331
Open your eyes.

875
00:55:31,331 --> 00:55:34,091
Please...

876
00:56:01,724 --> 00:56:04,202
I won't leave you alone.

877
00:56:04,202 --> 00:56:05,838
Wherever you go.

878
00:56:41,610 --> 00:56:42,778
Cut.

879
00:56:42,778 --> 00:56:44,377
Okay!

880
00:56:45,463 --> 00:56:46,929
Great job, everyone!

881
00:57:00,448 --> 00:57:02,178
Great job!

882
00:57:02,178 --> 00:57:03,726
Nice work.

883
00:57:04,598 --> 00:57:06,343
Good work, Director.

884
00:57:06,343 --> 00:57:07,553
Good work.

885
00:57:07,553 --> 00:57:08,784
I hardly did anything.

886
00:57:08,784 --> 00:57:10,764
You two did all the hard work.

887
00:57:10,764 --> 00:57:14,526
Thanks to you, the story I always dreamed of
finally came to life.

888
00:57:14,526 --> 00:57:15,945
Thank you.

889
00:57:17,272 --> 00:57:18,799
I'm glad.

890
00:57:19,392 --> 00:57:21,470
Now it's all up to me.

891
00:57:22,445 --> 00:57:27,142
The real work starts now.

892
00:57:28,952 --> 00:57:30,937
- Sorry?
- Huh?

893
00:57:32,112 --> 00:57:33,348
I mean the editing.

894
00:57:33,348 --> 00:57:35,025
Time to get started.

895
00:57:35,764 --> 00:57:37,255
Thanks again.

896
00:57:38,038 --> 00:57:39,451
Good job.

897
00:57:47,839 --> 00:57:50,842
Ha Na, you were amazing.

898
00:57:50,842 --> 00:57:51,843
Good job.

899
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:53,583
Good work. That's my star!

900
00:57:53,583 --> 00:57:55,680
- It's really over now.
- You did great.

901
00:57:55,680 --> 00:57:57,436
- Nice work!
- Thank you all!

902
00:57:57,436 --> 00:57:59,457
We left some things behind...

903
00:57:59,457 --> 00:58:00,898
Okay. I'll start the car.

904
00:58:00,898 --> 00:58:03,564
- Okay.
- See you in a bit.

905
00:58:05,067 --> 00:58:07,627
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

906
00:58:09,281 --> 00:58:10,493
Yeah?

907
00:58:11,667 --> 00:58:13,544
Can we talk for a second?

908
00:58:13,544 --> 00:58:15,154
Let's go!

909
00:58:15,154 --> 00:58:16,979
Hurry!

910
00:58:16,979 --> 00:58:19,035
Yeah... Sure.

911
00:58:22,894 --> 00:58:25,154
- Did you see this?
- What is it?

912
00:58:25,154 --> 00:58:27,038
It's from a fan...

913
00:58:27,038 --> 00:58:28,615
Oh, really?

914
00:58:33,383 --> 00:58:35,160
That must mean a lot.

915
00:58:35,160 --> 00:58:36,542
Yeah.

916
00:58:37,792 --> 00:58:39,710
- Want me to put it in the car?
- Yeah, I'll look at it later.

917
00:58:39,710 --> 00:58:41,374
- Okay.
- I'll go finish up too.

918
00:58:41,374 --> 00:58:42,680
- Okay.
- See you.

919
00:58:42,680 --> 00:58:44,196
See you later.

920
00:58:47,627 --> 00:58:49,093
Well...

921
00:58:50,080 --> 00:58:51,992
I saw the broadcast.

922
00:58:54,326 --> 00:58:55,718
Yeah.

923
00:58:56,575 --> 00:58:58,455
Did you mean what you said?

924
00:59:01,755 --> 00:59:02,945
You know...

925
00:59:02,945 --> 00:59:05,532
I finish really early tomorrow.

926
00:59:05,532 --> 00:59:07,556
"Really early?"

927
00:59:07,556 --> 00:59:09,516
Then what should we do tomorrow?

928
00:59:09,516 --> 00:59:10,753
Let's go get something good.

929
00:59:10,753 --> 00:59:12,321
What do you feel like?

930
00:59:12,966 --> 00:59:15,297
Let me think...

931
00:59:15,297 --> 00:59:17,211
Just name it.

932
01:00:26,627 --> 01:00:28,059
Ha Na.

933
01:00:28,910 --> 01:00:30,854
Ha Na... No...

934
01:00:30,854 --> 01:00:32,159
Ha Na.

935
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:34,756
Ha Na!

936
01:00:36,136 --> 01:00:37,609
Yoon Ha Na!

937
01:00:38,876 --> 01:00:40,334
- What's wrong?
- Ha Na!

938
01:00:40,334 --> 01:00:42,147
- Yoon Ha Na!
- Ha Na...

939
01:00:50,022 --> 01:00:51,380
119?

940
01:00:51,380 --> 01:00:52,806
We're at the Ilsan set...

941
01:00:52,806 --> 01:00:55,144
It's an emergency!

942
01:00:55,144 --> 01:00:56,670
No way...

943
01:01:00,793 --> 01:01:02,586
Woo Jae...

944
01:01:13,436 --> 01:01:15,282
I love you.

945
01:01:26,958 --> 01:01:28,556
Ha Na...

946
01:01:28,556 --> 01:01:30,516
This can't be...

947
01:01:34,238 --> 01:01:36,194
Ha Na, please...

948
01:01:36,194 --> 01:01:37,371
No...

949
01:01:38,118 --> 01:01:40,308
What's going on?

950
01:01:53,270 --> 01:01:54,756
What do we do...

951
01:02:44,155 --> 01:02:47,825
<i>Why can't anyone save you?</i>

952
01:02:47,825 --> 01:02:49,982
<i>Let's find a way.</i>

953
01:02:49,982 --> 01:02:51,835
<i>Somehow.</i>

954
01:02:51,835 --> 01:02:53,372
<i>Or...</i>

955
01:02:53,372 --> 01:02:55,592
<i>would you rather spend years in prison?</i>

956
01:02:55,592 --> 01:02:58,362
<i>The time machine isn't the camcorder...</i>

957
01:02:58,362 --> 01:03:00,238
<i>It's you?</i>

958
01:03:02,078 --> 01:03:03,882
<i>Yang Jun Mo, stop.</i>

959
01:03:03,882 --> 01:03:06,941
<i>You're ruining my work and my life.</i>

960
01:03:07,644 --> 01:03:10,684
<i>Aren't you curious how your story ends?</i>
